Commands in Lyntin are all located in the various modules
in the modules directory.  

To execute commands in the session you're currently in, just
execute the command.  To execute commands in another session,
type:
   #<session_name> <command...>

To execute a command in all the sessions, type:
   #all <command...>

To execute a command a number of times:
   #<number> <command...>

ex:
   #5 say hello
   #all say hello
   #all #alias {sh} {say hello}
